<strong>Pedicure cost</strong> sits anywhere between $20 and $100 or more, and almost none of that range is random. A basic pedicure at the neighbourhood salon and a deluxe spa treatment downtown are not the same service wearing different price tags. They are genuinely different products, built from different amounts of time, product, and technician attention. If you've ever paid sixty dollars for a mani-pedi and wondered whether you got taken for a ride, or paid twenty and worried you'd skipped something important, this guide settles it. We'll walk through exactly what <strong>pedicure cost</strong> looks like at each tier, what you're actually paying for, and how to know if your regular price is fair. This is part of our broader look at <a href="/blog/nail-costs/how-much-do-nails-cost">how much do nails cost</a>, where pedicures are just one piece of a bigger pricing picture.

