## How Much Does a Gel Pedicure Cost?

A gel pedicure costs $40 to $80 because the polish itself does more. A <strong>gel pedicure</strong> uses gel polish cured under UV or LED light, which holds its shine and resists chipping for two to four weeks. Regular polish, by comparison, usually starts looking tired after one to two weeks, especially on toes that spend all day in shoes.

That gap in longevity is the entire pitch. You're not paying more for a fancier-looking finish on day one, since gel and regular polish can look nearly identical fresh out of the salon. You're paying for the polish to still look fresh three weeks later, which matters more for feet than hands simply because toes get less daily wear and tear from washing, typing, and constant hand contact.

Removal adds a wrinkle worth knowing about upfront. Gel polish has to be soaked off rather than simply wiped away, and some salons charge a separate removal fee of $5 to $15 if you didn't get your last gel set there. Ask before you book if that matters to your budget.

