## What Affects How Much a Pedicure Costs

Why does the same service swing so wildly in price between two salons three streets apart? Rent is the biggest hidden factor, and it's the one most price guides skip past in favour of vaguer talk about "location." A salon paying premium downtown rent has to charge more per chair, full stop, regardless of how good the technician is.

Skill level and experience matter too, though less obviously. A technician with a decade of callus and ingrown nail experience commands a higher rate than someone new to the trade, the same way an experienced hairstylist charges more than a junior one for the identical haircut. Foot-specific issues, particularly stubborn calluses or early ingrown nails, take real time and care to handle properly, and that labour gets priced in.

Product quality plays a smaller but real role. Salons using higher-end scrubs, lotions, and polish brands pass some of that cost along. And it's worth understanding precisely <a href="/nail-faqs/whats-the-difference-between-a-manicure-and-a-pedicure">what actually separates a manicure from a pedicure treatment</a>, because pedicures generally take longer and involve more product than manicures at the same salon, which explains part of the price gap between the two services even before location enters the picture.

