## Pedicure Cost in the UK vs the US

Does currency change more than just the symbol? A basic <strong>pedicure cost</strong> in the UK runs £17 to £35, while the same tier in the US sits at $20 to $50. Once you account for the exchange rate, the ranges land close to each other, though UK pricing tends to sit slightly tighter at the lower end.

Salon pedicures in the UK climb to roughly £45, and a mani-pedi combination with gel colour can reach £80, numbers that track closely with what Airtasker UK reports as standard. The structure of the market looks similar on both sides of the Atlantic, basic, then spa, then gel, then combination packages, just denominated differently.

One real difference does matter for budgeting: in the US, <strong>pedicure</strong> prices vary enormously by region. A basic service in a smaller market can run $20, while the identical service in Manhattan or San Francisco often starts above $40 before you've added a single extra. The UK shows regional variation too, particularly between London and elsewhere, but the spread tends to be narrower. If you're trying to benchmark a US price against your area specifically, our <a href="/blog/nail-costs/nail-salon-cost-by-state">nail salon cost by state</a> breakdown goes deeper than a single national range can.

