## Mani-Pedi Combo Pricing: Do You Save Money?

Booking a manicure and pedicure together usually costs less than the sum of booking each separately, and the savings are real, not just a marketing trick. A typical mani-pedi combo runs $50 to $80, where booking a $25 manicure and a $35 pedicure on their own would total $60, before any combo discount applies.

The logic is straightforward from the salon's side. One client occupying one chair for a longer single appointment is more efficient than two separate bookings, two separate setups, two separate cleanups. That efficiency gets passed back as a modest discount, often 10 to 15 percent off the combined individual prices.

It's worth checking exactly what tier each half of the combo includes before assuming you're getting the best deal. A combo built from two basic services at $50 isn't actually cheaper than booking a $35 <a href="/blog/nail-costs/manicure-cost">how much does a manicure cost</a> manicure and a $35 basic pedicure separately if your salon's individual basic prices already run lower than their combo pricing suggests. Always compare the actual line items, not just the headline combo number.

