## The Real Answer Isn't a Number

A fair <strong>pedicure</strong> price isn't a fixed dollar figure, it's a match between what you're paying and what you're getting. $25 and $85 can both be perfectly reasonable, for entirely different services, at entirely different salons, and neither one is automatically the "right" price for everyone reading this.

What changes the equation is knowing which tier you're booking and why. Once you can name the difference between a basic service and a spa upgrade, between regular polish and gel, between a $20 strip-mall price and a $60 downtown one, the guesswork disappears. You stop comparing your bill to a vague internet average and start comparing it to the specific thing you actually received.

Next time you sit down in that chair, you'll know exactly what you're paying for, and whether it's worth it.
